    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the system of linear equations\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4u - 5v = 23 \\\\\n2u + 4v = -8\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nwe can use the method of elimination or substitution. Here, we'll use the elimination method.\n\nFirst, we'll multiply the second equation by 2 to align the coefficients of \\(u\\):\n\n\\[\n2 \\times (2u + 4v = -8) \\implies 4u + 8v = -16\n\\]\n\nNow we have the system:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4u - 5v = 23 \\\\\n4u + 8v = -16\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate \\(u\\):\n\n\\[\n(4u + 8v) - (4u - 5v) = -16 - 23\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\\[\n4u + 8v - 4u + 5v = -39\n\\]\n\nThis reduces to:\n\\[\n13v = -39\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(v\\):\n\\[\nv = \\frac{-39}{13}\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(v\\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(u\\). We'll use the second equation:\n\\[\n2u + 4v = -8\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(v = \\frac{-39}{13}\\):\n\\[\n2u + 4\\left(\\frac{-39}{13}\\right) = -8\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[\n2u - \\frac{156}{13} = -8\n\\]\n\nTo clear the fraction, multiply through by 13:\n\\[\n26u - 156 = -104\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(u\\):\n\\[\n26u = -104 + 156\n\\]\n\\[\n26u = 52\n\\]\n\\[\nu = \\frac{52}{26}\n\\]\n\\[\nu = 2\n\\]\n\nNow, we have \\(u = 2\\) and \\(v = \\frac{-39}{13}\\). To find \\(u + v\\):\n\\[\nu + v = 2 + \\left(\\frac{-39}{13}\\right)\n\\]\n\nConvert 2 to a fraction with the same denominator:\n\\[\nu + v = \\frac{26}{13} + \\left(\\frac{-39}{13}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nu + v = \\frac{26 - 39}{13}\n\\]\n\\[\nu + v = \\frac{-13}{13}\n\\]\n\\[\nu + v = -1\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(u + v\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]",
